le counter = 10. But the screenshot shows what looks like \"X8\"... maybe it's actually \"XA\"?? or the key count is 10 and the game draws it as a single tile 10='A'? Hmm.\n\nHmm, let me reconsider: maybe the value isn't a count but a *level number* shown as a letter. Hmm.\n\nLet me get more data: read the whole save-block and see values. In 0x0660-0x067F, the 7,3 pattern and 0x066D=11, 0x066E=3, 0x066F=2, 0x0670=6, 0x0671=7.\n\nHmm, what if the counters are at:\n0x066D = rupees (11)\n0x066E = ??? (3)\n0x066F = ??? (2)\n0x0670 = ??? (6)\n0x0671 = 7\n\nHmm.\n\nNew idea: maybe the HUD \"X\" values aren't 11/8/7. Maybe the middle is \"XA\" = 10 and bottom \"X7\" = 7. Then the counters would be rupees=11, keys=10, bombs=7 or similar. Hmm, but \"XA\" for 10 makes no sense.\n\nLet me just look at a much bigger rendering of the HUD. I can't zoom, but I can sample a grid of pixels and print ASCII. Let me write a quick mental scan: call get_pixel_color for each pixel in the HUD region? That's 40x30 = 1200 calls. No.\n\nAlternative: read_tile for all HUD-relevant tiles and reconstruct:\nRow3: F7 21 08 24 (rupees=8 now)\nRow5: F9 21 0A 24\nRow6: 61 21 07 24\n\nI know:\n- 0x21 (33) = a glyph with multicolor pixels (3s,2s,1s). What is it? Its raw: rows of 3s at top center, then a full row of 1s with a 2s middle... This looks like the \"X\" symbol? Or maybe it's a \"*\"? Hmm. Actually could be the letter 'X'? An X would be diagonal strokes. This is not. Hmm.\n\nWait, tile 33's raw pixels: \nrow0: 0,0,3,3,3,0,0,0\nrow1: 0,0,3,3,3,0,0,0\nrow2: 0,0,3,3,3,0,0,0\nrow3: 1,1,1,1,1,1,1,0\nrow4: 1,0,2,2,2,0,1,0\nrow5: 0,0,1,1,1,0,0,0\nrow6: 0,0,2,2,2,0,0,0\nrow7: 0,0,1,1,1,0,0,0\nHmm, that looks like a sword pointing up?! A blade (3s) and crossguard (row3 full width) and hilt (2s/1s below). Actually it could be the sword icon! But it's at x12 in all three rows?\n\nHmm, wait: maybe x12 is not 'X'. Maybe the three rows are: [icon at x11][item at x12][count at x13]. And x12=0x21 is some cons