0),(248,18),(252,18).\n\nHmm. Actually, let me reconsider: maybe the heart is at the LEFT of \"-LIFE-\"? In the screenshot, \"-LIFE-\" then heart on the right. Hmm.\n\nOK you know what, let me just reset and start a new game — that resolves the heart display and matches the task scene. Let me do that.\n\nReset → title. Then screenshot. Then press Start → file select. Then navigate.\n\nLet me reset.\n\nWait, the user said \"It starts on the title screen (a story scroll plays if you wait). Start on the title opens the file-select screen. To begin a new game there: press Select until the cursor is on REGISTER YOUR NAME and press Start; on the name screen press A once to enter a letter, then press Select until the cursor is on END and press Start; back on file select, press Select until the cursor is on the new file and press Start.\"\n\nLet me follow that.\n\nReset first.\n\nHmm, but actually, do I want to lose the current save (with rupees 11, etc.)? The task wants the first overworld screen of a new game. Let me proceed. But I've already got the addresses; a new game lets me verify hearts.\n\nActually, hmm, maybe I should NOT reset because the user's environment save might matter. But the user explicitly described starting a new game. And the file-select had one file already; starting a new game would use a second file (or overwrite?). \"press Select until the cursor is on the new file\" — implies there's a new file slot.\n\nHmm, wait, the earlier file-select screen showed a Triforce with one piece filled and an inventory — that might be the \"REGISTER YOUR NAME\" screen actually. Hmm.\n\nLet me just reset and see.\n\nActually, let me first save the current state (save_state) so I can come back. Slot 0 or 3.\n\nLet me save_state 3, then reset.\n\nLet me go.\n\nActually, hold on. Let me reconsider the heart issue once more before resetting, because I don't want to lose the ability to prove hearts via this save.\n\nThe heart display: no heart tiles/sprite. Maybe the sa